Physics based game where you need to keep a balancing disk from falling
	- you aim and throw objects using physics by setting weights which will affect drag and balancing of the disk
	- the shape chosen will be a shape
	- you set the size of the object
	- keep going as many times as you can
	- getting rid of objects by knocking them off the platform will not end the game but the higher number of items, the higher the score
Physics based game where your goal is to make the spring drop down with a heavy weight and stop right at the ground with miniscule recoil
	- either the spring constant, the distance to the ground, or the weight’s mass will be randomized. 2 of them can be but no more than 2
	- values randomized will not be changeable by the player
	- the player wins if the spring does not really jump back by a non-miniscule amount after dropping
	- Hooke's law will be visualized and the player will be helpful for the player filling in values
	- if a player does not succeed, let them retry with a point decrease. But after a few tries, allow them to skip for 1/3 of their points to be dropped instead of the full amount
Game where car is constantly moving down a path and the player needs to input values for x and y as the slope to set the car down a path to avoid crashing
	- the game will give the player some time to come up with values and visualize them when the car travels along
	- the player will be given the chance to look at what the line their values drew looked like and learn how the different values they gave form how steep a slope is
		- this will happen regardless of whether the player gave a successful slope or not
	- the game goes on forever until the player crashes
	- the closer the player gets a slope to the center of the road, the more points they will get
